      "title": "2. What Is Cognitive Development?",
      "order": 2,
      "hasVideo": false,
      "content": "> **Cognitive development:** Cognitive development means the way a child learns to think, understand, remember, pay attention, solve problems, and make sense of the world.\n\n\nIt includes skills such as:\n\n- Noticing and focusing on something\n- Remembering people, places, objects, and routines\n- Understanding cause and effect\n- Sorting, matching, counting, and comparing\n- Following simple instructions\n- Solving everyday problems\n- Using imagination and pretend play\n- Learning from experience\n\n\n> **Key Principle:** Cognitive development is closely connected with physical development, language, emotions, and relationships. A child who feels safe, loved, healthy, and well nourished is better able to explore, concentrate, and learn.\n\n\n> **Clinical Evidence:** WHO describes early learning as any opportunity for a child to interact with a person, place, or object in their environment. Every interaction contributes to brain development and lays a foundation for later learning.\n\n\n#### Growth and thinking\n\n**Example:** A child may grow taller, but cognitive development is seen when the child:\n\n- Recognizes their mother’s face\n- Looks for a toy hidden under a cloth\n- Understands that a cup is for drinking\n- Puts blocks into a container\n- Follows the instruction “Bring your shoes”\n- Asks, “Why is the sky blue?”\n- Pretends a banana is a telephone",
