      "order": 15,
      "hasVideo": false,
      "content": "### Common Mistakes Adults Make\n\n| Common Mistake | Recommended Evidence-Based Approach |\n| --- | --- |\n| **Doing everything for the child** | Give the child time to try, then offer help only when needed |\n| **Discouraging questions** | Answer simply and use questions as learning moments |\n| **Calling a child “slow” or “stubborn” when exploring** | Describe the behaviour positively: “You are curious” or “You are trying to understand how it works” |\n| **Comparing siblings or other children** | Focus on each child’s own progress and strengths |\n| **Expecting adult-level attention** | Keep activities short, playful, and suited to the child’s age |\n| **Using punishment instead of teaching** | Calmly redirect, explain, and give safe alternatives |\n| **Giving no opportunity for simple choices** | Offer limited choices, such as “red cup or blue cup?” |\n| **Relying entirely on screens for entertainment or learning** | Balance any screen use with play, conversation, movement, and stories |\n| **Assuming expensive toys are necessary** | Use safe household objects, stories, songs, and everyday activities |",
