      "title": "16. Practical Activity: “Think Like a Child”",
      "order": 16,
      "hasVideo": false,
      "content": "### Practical Activity: Think Like a Child\n\nChoose a safe everyday object, such as a plastic cup, spoon, lid, empty container, leaf, stone, or piece of cloth.\n\n**Sit with the child and explore the object together. Ask open questions such as:**\n\n- What do you think this is?\n- What do you think it does?\n- What happens if we put it inside this container?\n- Can you find another way to use it?\n- What do you think will happen next?\n- How are these two objects the same or different?\n\n> **Coaching Guidance:** Let the child touch, try, and explain their ideas. Do not rush to give the correct answer.\n\n#### Skills supported:\nThis activity supports:\n- Attention and observation\n- Curiosity\n- Language and communication\n- Memory\n- Problem-solving\n- Comparison and classification\n- Confidence and independent thinking\n\n**Infant Adaptation (0–12 Months):**\nFor babies, simplify the activity: show a safe object, name it, let the baby touch it, and describe what the baby is doing.",
